{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1554592-storypath","id":1554592,"title":"StoryPath","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-23T06:29:34-07:00","id":1554592,"title":"StoryPath","content":"Hope this wasn't answered elsewhere, but how self contained is Curseborne? Are all the rules to play in the core book? do you need the other StoryPath books, specifically Storypath Ultra and/or Trinity Continuum?<br /> <br /> if not is the Trinity book or the Storypath Ultra useful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25501-nina_blain","name":"nina_blain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T11:37:30-07:00","id":1554601,"title":"","content":"All the rules are in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T07:57:47-07:00","id":1554663,"title":"","content":"To elaborate, all the rules are in the core book, and Curseborne is its own completely self-contained setting. Curseborne's particular rules do <b>not</b> make it a simple matter to incorporate material from other game lines (like Trinity). For example, in Curseborne, players only really get to choose one of their Paths (the &quot;Role Path&quot; representing the character's more mundane aspects), and even then, the game presents a list of specific options as the default assumption - the option to draft your own Role Path is only given in a sidebar as a last-ditch stopgap for situations where none of the options given feel like they fit a specific real-world occupation in the eyes of both player and Storyguide.<br /> <br /> (EDIT: I should elaborate further: by &quot;only really get to choose one of their Paths,&quot; I mean that for many folklore monsters, deciding what kind of monster you are immediately locks in <b>two</b> paths, not one. Just the statement that your character is a werewolf automatically makes you Primal for Lineage Path, Get of Lyka for Family Path, for example. Vampires have it easier, since &quot;vampire&quot; gets an entire Lineage to itself, with a variety of Families of varied focus.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3388,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3388-r0gue_rob0t","user":"r0gue_rob0t","date":". 10-25-2025, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3388-r0gue_rob0t","name":"r0gue_rob0t","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T09:10:56-07:00","id":1554775,"title":"","content":"thanks guys <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25501-nina_blain","name":"nina_blain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}